To simulate, run:

make dummy_stratus-hls

make dummy_multicast_p2p_1_src-baremetal

TEST_PROGRAM=./soft-build/ariane/baremetal/dummy_multicast_p2p_1_src.exe

0 --- 1 --- 2
|     |     |
|     |     |
3 --- 4 --- 5
|     |     |
|     |     |
6 --- 7 --- 8

The chiplet system contains four 3x3 chiplets and five 2x2 chiplets, 9 accelerators, 4 memory tiles, 1 cpu tile, and 9 IO tiles.

Each chiplet contains an accelerator and chiplets 1, 3, 5, and 7 each contain one memory tile.
Also, there is one cpu in chiplet 4.
Lastly, each chiplet contains an IO tile.

The baremetal application instantiates two P2P communications in a 3x3 chiplet system.
Accelerator 8 requests data from accelerator 0 and accelerator 0 sends its data to accelerator 8.
Same operation occurs for accelerators 2 and 6. Accelerator 6 is the source.
